WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.570
SPEAKER: Welcome to this
episode of "Click to Deploy,"

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.730
a series where we
show you how easy it

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:09.400
is to deploy solutions from
the Google Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.950
In this episode,
I'll show you how

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.170
to set up an Apache
Cassandra database

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.320
deployment through
Google Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.630
Cassandra is an
open source NoSQL

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.760
distributed database
that is typically

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.590
used for training and inference
of deep neural networks.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.300
We'll start by
searching for Cassandra

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.280
in the GCP Marketplace.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.780
For the purpose
of this tutorial,

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.240
let's choose the Google
Click to Deploy a Cassandra

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.190
virtual machine.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.200
We are sent to this
landing page, which

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.680
shows us some very important
information about Cassandra,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.410
like an overview of
what Cassandra is,

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.030
details about the
virtual machine

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.640
and its operating system,
and most importantly,

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.660
the estimated monthly cost
of choosing this solution.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.630
Let's click the Launch button
to start this deployment.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.850
Now we get to choose some
important specifications

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.410
for our deployment.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.970
We'll start by naming our
deployment for this video.

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:03.510
We will name it cass-101.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.160
Next, we'll choose the zone.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.650
For this tutorial, I'll
keep the default zone.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.570
Then we can decide
on the cluster name.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:13.460
I'll choose the
default, Test Cluster.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.920
Next, we can determine
the instance count.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.725
I'll keep the count as the
default count of three.

00:01:18.725 --> 00:01:21.080
Next, we will
choose Machine type.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:24.620
For this video, I'll
use e2-highmem-4,

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.225
which are cost-optimized VMs.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.560
Finally, you can also decide
on other specifications

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.480
like network
interface, firewall,

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.440
and enable Stackdriver
logging and monitoring.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.330
Now that we've completed
the specifications,

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.350
we'll click the Deploy button.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:41.850
Great.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.950
So now our Cassandra
VM is deployed.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.870
And now, we see the
Deployment Manager.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.270
The Deployment Manager allows
you to create and manage

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.770
cloud resources.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.690
Here, we see the deployed
Cassandra instance,

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.780
which includes files that
show VM instance, disk,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.490
and firewall information.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:59.370
Now, we can test out
this Cassandra instance

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.578
by running a couple commands.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.840
There you have it-- a
Cassandra instance created

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.755
with a click of a button.

00:02:17.755 --> 00:02:19.880
If you enjoyed this video,
please subscribe and hit

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.100
the Like button.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.850
If you'd like to deploy
your own Cassandra

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.920
virtual machine
on your own, make

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.610
sure to click the
link down below.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:27.860
Thanks for watching.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:31.210
